{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's own claim of 29.13 km against a 21.9 km optimal route is confirmed by the platform's own GPS trace: the trace measures 29.13 km, an excess of 7.23 km over the booked optimal, which is 33.01% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass — the excess exceeds 20% of optimal and exceeds 0.8 km absolute — so the deviation is ESTABLISHED on this trip's own evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02831", "EV-TRIP-02831"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's asserted excuse — 'PIE was closed, LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-02831-01 covers it' — is weightless. The advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-02831-01 is MISSING from the bundle with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; no advisory covers the Blk 12 Telok Blangah Cres corridor in this window. Under POL-RD-13 the driver's external-traffic assertion is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else, and where the bundle holds no advisory covering the trip window, POL-RD-03 is unavailable and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The driver's assertion cites no evidence ID for an advisory, so the missing advisory is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact within POL-RD-10(5); it is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction in it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02831-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.advisories",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a) to (c): it carries 229 fixes at a 10-second sample interval with 100.0% coverage, zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds. The trace is COMPLETE at weight 1.0. The deviation therefore stands at the measured figure and POL-RD-02 runs against the booked optimal route; the driver's traffic assertion neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02831"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-13"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No rider-requested detour exonerates any part of the excess. The chat log for this trip is empty — 0 messages, first_message_at and last_message_at both null — so no rider instruction exists that could meet POL-RD-04(a) to (c), and no waypoint_hint is available to corroborate. POL-RD-04 is unavailable on the record and no distance is excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02831"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "message_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No pickup or dropoff relocation applies. The trip record shows original_pickup, original_dropoff, pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at all null, and amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min both null. POL-RD-05 cannot be run and no amended optimal route exists to re-apply POL-RD-01 against.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02831"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "amended_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip is not a pooled trip. The trip record shows vehicle_type RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null. POL-RD-12 does not apply and the baseline for POL-RD-01 remains the booked optimal of 21.9 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02831"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "relies_on": "vehicle_type",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs the refund arithmetic. Charged total is SGD 37.07. The recomputed fare on the booked optimal route is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 21.9 + 0.28 x 29.6) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP = SGD 29.3130. The refund is 37.07 - 29.3130 = SGD 7.7570, rounded up to SGD 7.80. This is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and below 90% of charged_total, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 7.80.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02831", "EV-TRIP-02831"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No ERP or toll pass-through correction is due. The fare breakdown carries zero ERP lines, zero tolls and zero airport surcharge, and the trip neither originates at an airport nor crosses any gantry. POL-RD-09 adds nothing to the POL-RD-02 refund and nothing is double-counted.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02831"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's profile does not establish a repeat deviation pattern under POL-RD-06. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1, below the threshold of 3, and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 271 is 0.0037, below the 0.05 ratio threshold. No POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral is available on this record, and the driver's lifetime prior_deviation_flags of 0 is context only under POL-GEN-01 and is not the trailing-90-day figure the clause asks for.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02831"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's profile does not trigger the POL-RD-08 corroboration requirement. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the threshold of 4, so the additional-corroboration condition for claims with excess below 30% is not engaged. The rider's claim is proven on the unimpaired GPS trace alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02831"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.7,
    "explanation": "Addressed to both parties. The deviation is proven, but the way the driver explains it invokes an exculpatory clause against an artifact that is not in the bundle, and that forces a human review: no money moves, and the contested SGD 9.00 is held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nThe trip. The platform GPS trace (EV-GPS-02831) measures 29.13 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff events; the booked optimal route (EV-TRIP-02831) is 21.9 km. The excess is 7.23 km, or 33.01% of optimal, so both POL-RD-01 tests pass (greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km absolute) and a route deviation is established. Under POL-RD-01 the trace figure governs, not the rounded 29.1 km on the trip record. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 229 fixes at 10-second spacing, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s, so POL-RD-10(3) does not apply. Nothing else rescues or adds to the excess: the chat log (EV-CHAT-02831) is empty, so no rider-requested detour exists (POL-RD-04); no pickup or dropoff was amended (POL-RD-05); the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so the solo/pooled baseline is not in play (POL-RD-12); and no repeat-deviation pattern is established (deviation_flags_90d = 1 against 271 completed trips, below both POL-RD-06 thresholds), so no conduct referral fires. On the METERED fare (EV-FARE-02831), the POL-RD-02 arithmetic would be recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 21.9 + 0.28 x 29.6) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP = SGD 29.3130 against a charged_total of SGD 37.07, a refund of 7.7570 rounded up to SGD 7.80, and nothing is added under POL-RD-09 because there are no ERP, toll or surcharge lines.\n\nWhy I cannot pay it. The driver explains the route by 'PIE was closed, LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-02831-01 covers it.' That advisory is present in the bundle only as a MISSING artifact - admissibility status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - so POL-RD-03 cannot be run against it and the excuse carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Critically, because the driver cited that missing identifier as his ground, POL-RD-13(1) expressly does not narrow POL-RD-10(5): an exculpatory clause (POL-RD-03) has been invoked against a cited artifact (EV-ADVIS-02831-01) that is missing from the pool. POL-RD-10(5) is a mandatory escalation trigger, and escalation under POL-RD-10 is terminal - it replaces the ruling, both money fields are null, and the disputed amount is held.\n\nWhat would resolve it: a traffic_advisory covering this trip window that names a road or segment the optimal route traverses, carries a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle would have reached it, and states the shortest lawful alternative distance so the POL-RD-03 exoneration cap can be computed; or the driver withdrawing the closure assertion, in which case the deviation stands at 7.23 km and the POL-RD-02 partial refund of SGD 7.80 is the arithmetic result.\n\nOn the claims. The rider's claim that the driver 'cites no evidence ID for an advisory' misstates the record - the driver's statement names EV-ADVIS-02831-01 - and is rejected on that ground. The rider's further argument that the absent advisory cannot escalate was discarded by the referee with reason IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED and is not reinstated. Both sides' claims on the trace, the establishment tests, the fare arithmetic, the empty chat log, the absence of relocation or pooling, and the profile evidence are accepted; they do not change the outcome because the escalation is procedural. Every profile field mentioned (prior_deviation_flags, prior_no_show_flags and the rest) is context only under POL-GEN-01 and grounds nothing. Confidence is 0.70, the policy floor, because the escalation turns on a missing artifact that carries no weight of its own. No clause produces a referral, so the referrals list is empty."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver's traffic excuse does not escalate this case. He cited the missing advisory identifier, but the artifact is absent from the bundle rather than contradicted by it, and the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c): 229 fixes at a 10.0 s sample interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0. POL-RD-13(2) therefore applies — the deviation stands at the measured figure and POL-RD-02 runs against the booked optimal route, with the assertion recorded as discarded and no advisory on file.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02831-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: I have not decided this dispute, and no money moves today. The case goes to a human reviewer, because POL-RD-10(5) is triggered.\n\nWhat I accepted. The platform's own GPS trace for TRP-02831 is intact — 229 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps, maximum gap 0 seconds — so it is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and is NOT impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a) to (c). (Schema status and policy impairment are two different tests, and this trace passes both.) The deviation measured on it is therefore reliable: the trace runs 29.13 km against a booked optimal route of 21.9 km, an excess of 7.23 km, or 33.01%. Both POL-RD-01 tests pass (greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km absolute), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED on this trip's own evidence. I also accepted that no rider-requested detour applies (the chat log holds 0 messages, so POL-RD-04 has nothing to run on), that no pickup or dropoff relocation applies (original and amended endpoint fields are all null, POL-RD-05), that the trip is not pooled (vehicle_type RYDE_X, so the 21.9 km booked optimal is the right baseline, POL-RD-12), and that there is no ERP, toll or airport-surcharge line to correct (all nil, POL-RD-09 — nothing is added on top of, or double-counted against, any distance refund).\n\nThe trigger that fired — POL-RD-10(5), an exculpatory clause invoked against an artifact missing from the pool. In his statement of 8 September 2026 the driver wrote: 'PIE was closed, LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-02831-01 covers it.' He named that advisory by its evidence ID as the ground of his POL-RD-03 exoneration. That matters, because it is not an uncited assertion of bad traffic. EV-ADVIS-02831-01 sits in the bundle with admissibility status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (no advisory covers the Blk 12 Telok Blangah Cres corridor in this window) and weight_multiplier 0.0; a MISSING artifact carries no fact, and its absence is what is citable. POL-RD-13 tests an external-traffic excuse against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else, and no advisory on file covers this window, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run. But POL-RD-13(1) draws its line exactly here: where the asserting party names no evidence ID for an advisory, the missing advisory is a gap in the bundle and not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation; where the party DOES cite the missing identifier, POL-RD-10(5) is not narrowed and the case still escalates. The driver cited it. The trigger fires, and under POL-RD-10 escalation is terminal.\n\nClaims answered. The rider's claim and the driver's claim that this does not escalate are rejected: both rest on the assertion that the driver's excuse cites no evidence ID, and the record shows he cited EV-ADVIS-02831-01 by name. The POL-RD-13(2) route the rider's side proposed — deviation stands, POL-RD-02 runs — would have applied had the advisory been cited by nobody; it does not survive POL-RD-13(1). For the reviewer's information only, that arithmetic would be: charged_total $37.07 less a recomputed optimal-route fare of $29.3130 (base $3.80 + $0.75 x 21.9 km + $0.28 x 29.6 min, surge x1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, + $0.80 platform fee, no ERP or surcharge), giving $7.7570, rounded up to $7.80, above the $0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share. No amount is ordered: amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd are null and the $9.00 in dispute is held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nNo referral issues. Both POL-RD-06 claims are accepted — driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against completed_trips_90d of 271 (ratio 0.0037), below both POL-RD-06 thresholds — so there is no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c); the deviation is not 'material' in any event (33.01% and 7.23 km fall short of 50% and 8.0 km), and the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context only under POL-GEN-01. There is no phantom gantry or surcharge line, so POL-RD-09(4) does not fire. The rider's profile does not engage the POL-RD-08 corroboration gate (deviation_claims_60d is 1, below 4), and the no-show counters on both profiles are context only. The referrals list is empty.\n\nWhat would resolve it. The reviewer needs the LTA traffic-advisory source for the PIE / Blk 12 Telok Blangah Cres corridor covering 7 September 2026, 16:02-16:49: its identifier, the road or segment it names, its validity window, and the shortest lawful alternative distance. With that, POL-RD-03 can be run in full, or the advisory can be confirmed absent and the case closed on the measured deviation. Absent that record, no finding is made against either party."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
